    "answer": {
      "short": "$a^3+b^3+c^3-3abc$.\n\nDistribute each of $a$, $b$ and $c$; opposite mixed terms cancel, leaving three $-abc$ terms.",
      "worked": "Distribute each term of the first factor:\n$$\\begin{align*}(a+b+c)(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ac)&=a(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ac)\\\\&\\quad+b(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ac)\\\\&\\quad+c(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ac).\\end{align*}$$\nThe three products are\n$$\\begin{align*}a(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ac)&=a^3+ab^2+ac^2-a^2b-abc-a^2c,\\\\b(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ac)&=a^2b+b^3+bc^2-ab^2-b^2c-abc,\\\\c(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ac)&=a^2c+b^2c+c^3-abc-bc^2-ac^2.\\end{align*}$$\nAdd these expressions. Opposite mixed terms cancel and the three $-abc$ terms combine:\n$$(a+b+c)(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ac)=a^3+b^3+c^3-3abc.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
